<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ziyadat Allah III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 916</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ziyadat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> III was the last Aghlabid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>, who came to power in 903 after having his father, Abdallah II, murdered. He could not stop the advance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutama-berbers">Kutama Berbers</a> under the Fatimid missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-abdallah-al-shii">Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i</a>, and in 909 he fled east with his treasure. He died in exile, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> was proclaimed in his former lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ziyadat-allah-iii.jpg" alt="Ziyadat Allah III" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aghlabid_dinar_-_Ziyadat_Allah_III.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
